{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so our ADK support agent on Cloud Run went into a loop last night calling lookup_order like 400 times on one conversation and we ate a nasty Vertex bill. I need: max tool calls + max LLM turns per request, a daily token budget per user, and when our monthly budget gets low it should degrade (switch to flash, then disable expensive tools, then read-only mode) instead of just dying. Where do I hook this in ADK — callbacks? plugin? Show me code pls, demo for leadership is Friday."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "We are building a finance-ops agent with Google ADK (Python 3.12, deployed to Agent Engine). Some tools issue refunds over $500 or modify vendor bank details, and compliance requires a human approver to sign off before execution. The approval may take hours, so the agent session must pause and resume once someone approves or rejects in our internal Slack bot. We also need an immutable audit trail (who approved, when, which tool call args), probably in BigQuery or Firestore. Separately, I'd like per-session step limits so the agent can't wander indefinitely. Could you propose an architecture and the key ADK pieces (before_tool_callback, long-running tools, session state?) with sample code?"},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "my ADK agent is super slow and burns tokens because every turn it re-sends the whole 40-page policy doc in the system prompt. how do I stop that? context caching? RAG? something else? latency is like 9s per reply rn", "needs_instead": "Prompt/context optimization: moving the large document into Vertex AI context caching or a retrieval (RAG) tool to cut per-turn tokens and latency, not runtime caps, budgets, or human approval gates."}
]}
